> [!NOTE]
> This proposal depends on the Navigator proposal (#69967, PR #69968) and on the internal `FeatureContext` change (#69993). No review is needed yet. I will ask for a review after those are settled, and I will update this proposal if they change.

## Background and Motivation

`Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Platform` (#69304) gives Blazor applications typed access to standard browser APIs. This proposal adds the Storage API (`navigator.storage`) for the storage management family (#69875).

Applications that keep data in the browser, such as in IndexedDB or Cache Storage, need two things from this API.

- They can show how much storage they use and how much they can use (`estimate()`).
- They can ask the browser not to clear their data under storage pressure (`persist()`), and check whether it is kept (`persisted()`).

Today they need `IJSRuntime` for that.

`StorageManager` hangs off `Navigator`, so it builds on the Navigator proposal (#69967). A proof of concept is on my fork, in the branch [`components-platform-storage-manager`](https://github.com/jsakamotoIGJP/aspnetcore/tree/components-platform-storage-manager). It is stacked on the Navigator branch, and the change for this family is in [one commit](https://github.com/jsakamotoIGJP/aspnetcore/commit/9e5bc7264fc1a86be3025fbe5501ea4e67e6428f). I will not open a pull request until the Navigator and `FeatureContext` pull requests are merged. The branch will be cleaned up then, and it may be rebased.

## Usage Examples

```csharp
builder.Services.AddBrowserPlatform();
```

```razor
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Platform
@inject IBrowserPlatform Browser

<p>Used: @estimate?.Usage of @estimate?.Quota bytes</p>
<p>Persistent: @persisted</p>
<button @onclick="PersistAsync">Keep my data</button>

@code {
    private StorageEstimate? estimate;
    private bool persisted;

    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
    {
        if (firstRender)
        {
            estimate = await Browser.Window.Navigator.Storage.EstimateAsync();
            persisted = await Browser.Window.Navigator.Storage.PersistedAsync();
            StateHasChanged();
        }
    }

    private async Task PersistAsync()
    {
        persisted = await Browser.Window.Navigator.Storage.PersistAsync();
    }
}
```

The API works in Interactive Server and WebAssembly.

## Proposed API

```diff
 namespace Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Platform;

+public sealed class StorageManager
+{
+    public ValueTask<bool> PersistedAsync();
+    public ValueTask<bool> PersistAsync();
+    public ValueTask<StorageEstimate> EstimateAsync();
+}
+
+public sealed class StorageEstimate
+{
+    public ulong? Usage { get; init; }
+    public ulong? Quota { get; init; }
+}
+
+public static class NavigatorStorageManagerExtensions
+{
+    extension(Navigator navigator)
+    {
+        public StorageManager Storage { get; }
+    }
+}
```

The names and types follow the Web IDL of the [Storage Standard](https://github.com/w3c/webref/blob/main/ed/idl/storage.idl). `navigator.storage` is `[SameObject]`, so it becomes a synchronous property. `unsigned long long` becomes `ulong`. The members of `StorageEstimate` are not `required` in Web IDL, so they are nullable.

`StorageManager` works like `Storage` and `CookieStore`. Every caller gets the same instance from `Navigator.Storage`, and the DI scope disposes it.

`navigator.storage` exists only in a secure context. When it is missing, every method throws `NotSupportedException`, as `CookieStore` does.

Two members are left out on purpose.

- `getDirectory()`, which the File System standard adds to `StorageManager`. It returns a `FileSystemDirectoryHandle`, which needs its own family and the design for objects that the application owns.
- `usageDetails`, which Chromium adds to the result of `estimate()`. It is a Chromium-only property and is not in the Web IDL.

## Alternative Designs

Applications can keep using `IJSRuntime`, such as `JS.InvokeAsync<bool>("navigator.storage.persist")`.

The property could be named `StorageManager` to avoid confusion with the Web Storage `Storage` type. I kept `Storage`, because it is the Web IDL name and developers who know `navigator.storage` look for it.

The extension class is named after the type it returns (`NavigatorStorageManagerExtensions`), not after the property (`NavigatorStorageExtensions`). This also avoids confusion with Web Storage. I plan to propose this as a rule for all families in a later update of the porting skill.

## Risks

All three methods are Baseline widely available, so none of them is `[Experimental]`.

Like Web Storage, the API is unavailable before interactivity.

## Source Justifications

- The family covers `estimate()`, `persist()`, and `persisted()`: "Expose browser storage estimates and persistence controls." (#69875)
- Applications reach it from `Navigator`: "`Browser.Navigator.Storage`" (#69875)
- `navigator.storage` is the same object for the life of the page and exists only in a secure context: "`[SecureContext] interface mixin NavigatorStorage { [SameObject] readonly attribute StorageManager storage; };`" ([storage.idl](https://github.com/w3c/webref/blob/main/ed/idl/storage.idl))
- The members of `StorageEstimate` are optional `unsigned long long`, and `usageDetails` is not one of them: "`dictionary StorageEstimate { unsigned long long usage; unsigned long long quota; };`" ([storage.idl](https://github.com/w3c/webref/blob/main/ed/idl/storage.idl))
- `getDirectory()` comes from another specification: "`partial interface StorageManager { Promise<FileSystemDirectoryHandle> getDirectory(); };`" ([fs.idl](https://github.com/w3c/webref/blob/main/ed/idl/fs.idl))
- The methods are Baseline widely available: "`baseline: high`", "`baseline_high_date: 2026-03-18`" (`storage-manager` in [web-features](https://github.com/web-platform-dx/web-features))
- The API works in Interactive Server and WebAssembly: "`StorageManagerPaths = ["/storagemanager-server", "/storagemanager-wasm"]`" (`StorageManagerTests.cs`)

